  "scope": "The literal1220-slot program constructs the grid metadata from the original cost row, reads its actual indexed cost, computes the original lambda, and passes that same returned fraction root into the actual scalar-addition row on the same heap. The exact original shifted cost row is returned in both rational-list and original two-word table representations. No dimension, width, fuel, selected cost, lambda result or shifted row is supplied. The universal trace retains the original row/index/exponent and pays every child call, allocation and terminal halt. Its bound uses only original row bits/count and index/exponent lengths and numerical exponent; the explicit grid-range corollary removes numerical-exponent dependence using the proved original limit. The later loop must establish that range invariant. Valid original index, input representations/H/A and dense cursor remain supplied. Minimum selection and complete guess/solver composition remain separate. Twelve physical cases independently specify every unreduced raw output fraction, including zeros, duplicates and padded inputs.",
  "pending": [
    "independent semantic review",
    "combined production integration and exact CI"
  ]
